  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}$ bond angle is about $120^{\\circ}$, when $\\mathrm{C}$ is bonded through a double bond but in case of $\\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ the $\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}$ bond angle is only $109^{\\circ} \\mathrm{2B}^{\\prime}$\r\nCyclic compounds have a $\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}$ bond angle Feater than $109^{\\circ} 28^{\\prime}$ due to hindrance. Thus, the correct order of $1 \\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}$ bond angle is\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2014_che_a8.png\">",
